{"id":"a10","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":15,"of":16,"title":"Counting","titleHe":"מִסְפָּרִים","goal":"Count to ten — and pick the right set of numbers.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew numbers have two sets, and the one you use depends on the gender of what you're counting. This catches every learner: the form that looks feminine, ending in ־ָה, is the one used with masculine nouns."},{"type":"table","caption":"One to ten","head":["","with feminine nouns","with masculine nouns"],"rows":[["1","אַחַת","אֶחָד"],["2","שְׁתַּיִם","שְׁנַיִם"],["3","שָׁלוֹשׁ","שְׁלוֹשָׁה"],["4","אַרְבַּע","אַרְבָּעָה"],["5","חָמֵשׁ","חֲמִשָּׁה"],["6","שֵׁשׁ","שִׁשָּׁה"],["7","שֶׁבַע","שִׁבְעָה"],["8","שְׁמוֹנֶה","שְׁמוֹנָה"],["9","תֵּשַׁע","תִּשְׁעָה"],["10","עֶשֶׂר","עֲשָׂרָה"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"Counting out loud — one, two, three with nothing being counted — uses the feminine set. So does giving a phone number."},{"type":"tip","body":"One is the exception to the exception: it follows its noun like an adjective. סֵפֶר אֶחָד, one book. Every other number comes first: שְׁלוֹשָׁה סְפָרִים."}],"vocab":[{"he":"אֶחָד","en":"one (m.)","translit":"echad"},{"he":"שְׁנַיִם","en":"two (m.)","translit":"shnayim"},{"he":"שְׁלוֹשָׁה","en":"three (m.)","translit":"shlosha"},{"he":"אַרְבָּעָה","en":"four (m.)","translit":"arba'a"},{"he":"חֲמִשָּׁה","en":"five (m.)","translit":"chamisha"},{"he":"עֲשָׂרָה","en":"ten (m.)","translit":"asara"},{"he":"מִסְפָּר","en":"number","translit":"mispar"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["is sorry","truth","fridge","one (m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"אֶחָד","translit":"echad"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["moon","lives, resides","eighty","two (m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"שְׁנַיִם","translit":"shnayim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["three (m.)","kilo","mentions, reminds","travels, strolls"],"correct":0,"prompt":"שְׁלוֹשָׁה","translit":"shlosha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["bee","four (m.)","autumn","wife, woman"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אַרְבָּעָה","translit":"arba'a"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["earth, ground","asks","with him","five (m.)"],"correct":3,"prompt":"חֲמִשָּׁה","translit":"chamisha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["ten (m.)","tall, high","beginning","reason, cause"],"correct":0,"prompt":"עֲשָׂרָה","translit":"asara"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["green (f.)","angry","was (f.)","number"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מִסְפָּר","translit":"mispar"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “four (m.)”?","options":["כַּמּוּת","גּוֹרָל","אַרְבָּעָה","מִסְפָּר"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["שְׁלוֹשָׁה","שְׁנַיִם","מִסְפָּר","עֲשָׂרָה"],"correct":1,"say":"שְׁנַיִם","he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["שְׁנַיִם","עֲשָׂרָה","שְׁלוֹשָׁה","אַרְבָּעָה"],"correct":3,"say":"אַרְבָּעָה","he":true},{"type":"read","he":"שְׁנַיִם","translit":"shnayim","en":"two (m.)"},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “number”?","options":["מֶלֶךְ","טִפֵּשׁ","מְדִינָה","מִסְפָּר"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["אַרְבָּעָה","מִסְפָּר","שְׁנַיִם","עֲשָׂרָה"],"correct":1,"say":"מִסְפָּר","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “five (m.)”?","options":["כֶּסֶף","תִּקְוָה","בֵּינְתַיִם","חֲמִשָּׁה"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אֶחָד","one (m.)"],["שְׁנַיִם","two (m.)"],["שְׁלוֹשָׁה","three (m.)"],["אַרְבָּעָה","four (m.)"],["חֲמִשָּׁה","five (m.)"]]},{"type":"type","q":"Write “two (m.)” in Hebrew","answer":"שְׁנַיִם","hint":"shnayim"}]}